# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (CLAUDE.md, "Sanitizers"). Run with
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp
#
# SQLite's WAL index ("-shm", shared memory) is read without locks by design: connections
# coordinate through file locks (fcntl) and memory barriers, which ThreadSanitizer doesn't
# see. Two connections writing in turn (one per drive worker) then look like a race inside
# these functions. Only SQLite's own wal-index functions are listed, so races in hoardor's
# code still show.
race:walIndexWriteHdr
race:walIndexTryHdr
race:walIndexReadHdr
race:walTryBeginRead
race:walIndexAppend
race:walCheckpoint

# libmpv's decoding: ffmpeg's frame-threaded decoders (libavcodec, libavutil) inside libmpv
# synchronize with atomics in code built without ThreadSanitizer, so the tool reports their
# buffer handover between decoder threads as races (2026-10-03: 13 reports in the player
# tests, all with frames only in libmpv/libavcodec/libavutil, none in hoardor). Matched by
# module, so races with a hoardor frame still show.
race:libavcodec.so
race:libavutil.so
race:libmpv.so
